<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#elector-palatine">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elector Palatine</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Elector of the Palatinate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elector Palatine was the title of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/count-palatine">Count Palatine</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> as one of the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356">Golden Bull of 1356</a>. The office was held by the Wittelsbach family, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg">Heidelberg</a>, and passed between its branches such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simmern">Simmern</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neuburg-an-der-donau">Neuburg</a> as lines died out. Elector Frederick V's acceptance of the Bohemian crown in 1619 helped start <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War.</p></div>
